    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d143">

                <pb facs="0252" n="148" xml:id="pg148"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/1253.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Minister.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-01-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 24, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Department learns from the American group that the consortium is not
                    threatened by the proposed advance to be made independently by the British and
                    German bankers, but that this advance if made would be open to participation by
                    the other groups as required by the quadruple and sextuple inter-group
                    agreements.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
